Using the difference of squares, we have \begin{align*}
\left(a+\frac{1}{b}\right)\left(\frac{1}{b}-a\right) &= \left(a^2+\frac{1}{b^2}-a^2\right) \\
&= \frac{1}{b^2} \\
&= \frac{1}{25} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{1}{25}}.
\end{align*}. The answer is \frac{1}{25}

