25 &= 30 - C\cap C
\end{align*}
We can then solve for $C\cap C$:
\begin{align*}
C\cap C &= 5
\end{align*}
We also know that $P\cap P = 75$, so $P\cap C = 50$.  Since $P\cap C = 75$, we can set up the following equation:
\begin{align*}
P\cap C &= 75 \\
50 &= 75 - P\cap P
\end{align*}
We can then solve for $P\cap P$:
\begin{align*}
P\cap P &= 25
\end{align*}
We can now set up the following equation:
