\[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c) = \frac{1}{16}(b-c)^2(a+b+c)(a+b-c)(a-b+c),\]which simplifies to
\[\frac{1}{16}(b-c)^2(a+b+c)(a+b-c)(a-b+c) = s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c).\]Since $s$ is the semiperimeter, we have $s = \frac{a+b+c}{2},$ so
