To simplify the expression $(u+4)(u-1) - (u-3)(u+6)$, we will first expand each product separately and then combine like terms.

1. Expand $(u+4)(u-1)$:
\begin{align*}
(u+4)(u-1) &= u^2 - u + 4u - 4 \\
&= u^2 + 3u - 4
\end{align*}

2. Expand $(u-3)(u+6)$:
\begin{align*}
(u-3)(u+6) &= u^2 + 6u - 3u - 18 \\
&= u^2 + 3u - 18
\end{align*}

3. Combine the expanded forms:
\begin{align*}
(u^2 + 3u - 4) - (u^2 + 3u - 18) &= u^2 + 3u - 4 - u^2 - 3u + 18 \\
&= 14
\end{align*}

Therefore, the simplified expression is $\boxed{14}$.

