To find the magnitude of $w$, we can use the formula $|w| = \sqrt{\text{Re}(w)^2 + \text{Im}(w)^2}$, where $\text{Re}(w)$ and $\text{Im}(w)$ are the real and imaginary parts of $w$, respectively.
Let's find the real and imaginary parts of $w$.
\begin{align*}
\text{Re}(w) &= \frac{3}{5} \cdot \text{Re}(z) - \frac{1}{5} \cdot \text{Im}(z) \\
&= \frac{3}{5} \cdot 1 - \frac{1}{5} \cdot 1 \\
&= \frac{2}{5} \\
\text{Im}(w) &= \frac{3}{5} \cdot \text{Im}(z) + \frac{1}{5} \cdot \text{Re}(z) \\
&= \frac{3}{5} \cdot 1 + \frac{1}{5} \cdot 1 \\
&= \frac{4}{5}
\end{align*}
Now we can find the magnitude of $w$:
\begin{align*}
|w| &= \sqrt{\text{Re}(w)^2 + \text{Im}(w)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{\left(\frac{2}{5}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{4}{25} + \frac{16}{25}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{20}{25}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{4}{5}} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}}
\end{align*}
The answer is: \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}
